-- TYPICALLY defaults are meaningless on a TYPE binder (a type variable, or a
-- type declared open for a section): a "default value" for a type makes no
-- sense, so it is rejected rather than silently dropped.

-- ERROR: TYPICALLY on a type declared by a section GIVEN (the same error the
-- deprecated `ASSUME \`some type\` IS A TYPE TYPICALLY 42` reported)
§ `Type binders`
    GIVEN `some type` IS A TYPE TYPICALLY 42

-- ERROR: TYPICALLY on a TYPE parameter
GIVEN a IS A TYPE TYPICALLY 42
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `bad type param` IF TRUE
